## Culprit hunk

No hunk confirmed. Cleared: 0086, 0082 (both hunks), 0085, 0084, 0083+0085, whole metal dir, llama-quant. Every variant = 276, i.e. beta 8.

Pin-based bisect invalid: pin lacks the model's own type.

```
pin  ggml/include/ggml.h    PQ2_0 refs: 0    HEAD: 2
pin  ggml/src/ggml-common.h block_pq2_0: 0   HEAD: 2
```

`GGML_TYPE_PQ2_0` / `block_pq2_0` / `dequantize_row_pq2_0` come from `731b358fd`. Reverting `ggml/` to pin will not compile against series consumers (`ggml.c` `GGML_OP_COUNT` static assert, `ggml-backend.cpp:437` `read_batch_begin`, `src/llama-context.cpp:965` `ggml_backend_sched_share_compute_buffers`, `src/models/delta-net-base.cpp:437` `ggml_gated_delta_net_set_raw_gates`). beta.7's engine is a sibling branch that already has PQ2_0, not this pin.

Leading candidate: `ggml/src/ggml-quants.c:494` `dequantize_row_pq2_0`, `ggml/src/ggml-common.h:199-200` (`QK_PQ2_0 128`, one fp16 scale per 128 weights), plus `ggml/src/ggml-cpu/` PQ2_0 vec-dot. Needs a PQ2_0-preserving partial revert, not a revert.

## Verdict

No correctness bug. band16 (309) and band1100 (255) are byte-identical between beta.7 and beta 8; only band300 differs, one token at char 226:

```
b7: ... Need answer one word. Likely blue. Need be terse. ...
b8: ... Need answer one word. Likely "blue". Need be terse. ...
```

Same word, different punctuation token = near-tie logits cut differently. A real kernel/quant bug moves text at every prompt length; here the 125-token and long prompts are clean. `envoff` also kills the op-offload explanation: beta 8 binary with offload disabled still emits beta 8's text.

